  "reason": "The strongest evidence is that multimodal multiprofile with PCA, avgpool, and weighted fusion is the best-performing family so far, with config_019 reaching 0.639 validation accuracy and 0.620 F1. The image encoder is an important untested factor in this best family, and the image-only ResNet50 baseline was weak, suggesting that a stronger pretrained image encoder may help the image branch contribute more effectively. config_025 tests exactly this by keeping the proven multiprofile avgpool weighted PCA setup and replacing ResNet50 with imagenet_vit_l. It is the best next experiment because it directly exploits the current strongest direction while clarifying whether image-encoder quality is a key source of remaining performance."
